# libpdx-argv — consumers.list
#
# Authoritative list of downstream repos that link and call this library.
# Format: <repo>/<path> — <symbols-called>
#
# Derived from README §Callers (libpdx-argv.ENH-011 audit, 2026-08-25;
# refreshed at 2026-09-02 for the ENH-030 rename):
# each entry was verified by grepping the tool's own src/ for calls into
# this library's exported symbols (parse_argv, parsed_args_reset,
# flag_spec_reset, flag_spec_register, register_all,
# parse_from_schema_record, fill_doc_argv, schema_emit_reset,
# schema_emit_register).
#
# When adding a consumer, append a new line here AND update README §Callers
# with the same information (this file is authoritative; README mirrors it
# in prose). Removing a consumer requires both this file and README to be
# updated in the same commit.
#
# Comments (# ...) and blank lines are ignored by any downstream tooling
# that consumes this file (e.g., pkg/deps.list validators).

paideia-os/pkg/src/main.pdx:103                    — parse_argv (dispatches on ParsedArgs::pos_ptrs[0])
paideia-os/ls/src/argv_surface.pdx:223,228,263     — parsed_args_reset, parse_argv (branches on ParsedArgs::emit_schema)
paideia-os/cp/src/main.pdx:125,141                 — register_all, parse_argv
paideia-os/mkdir/src/mkdir.pdx:1210                — parse_argv
paideia-os/mv/src/argv.pdx:194                     — parse_argv
paideia-os/rm/src/main.pdx:130                     — parse_argv

# R90-XREPO satellite cascade (ENH-030 rename adoption, 2026-09-02):
# three volume-tooling satellites migrated their handwritten argv
# scanners onto libpdx-argv. Each satellite's src/argv.pdx keeps its
# same public entry point (argv_parse) as a thin wire-in shim that
# calls flag_spec_reset + flag_spec_register (per-flag) + parsed_args_
# reset + parse_argv, then walks ParsedArgs::flag_ids[]/flag_values[]/
# pos_ptrs[] once to populate the caller's fixed-offset ParsedArgv
# struct. mkfs.pdxfs uses parse_int_u64 for --journal-size /
# --passphrase-fd; mount.pdxfs uses it for --snapshot / --passphrase-fd.
mkfs.pdxfs/src/argv.pdx                            — flag_spec_reset, flag_spec_register (x11), parsed_args_reset, parse_argv, parse_int_u64 (x2), flag_count, flag_ids, flag_values, pos_count, pos_ptrs
mount.pdxfs/src/argv.pdx                           — flag_spec_reset, flag_spec_register (x8), parsed_args_reset, parse_argv, parse_int_u64 (x2), flag_count, flag_ids, flag_values, pos_count, pos_ptrs
umount.pdxfs/src/argv.pdx                          — flag_spec_reset, flag_spec_register (x4), parsed_args_reset, parse_argv, flag_count, flag_ids, pos_count, pos_ptrs

# Total: 9 consumers — 6 P0 tools of the R49+R50 sweep plus the 3
# R90-XREPO volume-tooling satellites. The three remaining P0 tools
# (cat, doc, shell) are documented in README §Callers as non-callers
# with their reasons (scheduled M3 migration, planned M2 migration,
# and libpdx-argv.ENH-006 caller-owned-context prerequisite
# respectively).
